dxmt: Skip a frame the layer gives no drawable for, keeping its fences.

Presenter::encodeCommands used CAMetalLayer's nextDrawable unchecked. macOS returns no drawable
for a layer of no size and when the wait for one times out; the render pass was then made with no
texture and the command buffer presented nothing, which Metal takes as an error.

encodeCommands now returns at once when there is no drawable. The Present encoder then still
waits for and updates the frame's fences, in a blit encoder, because later encoders wait for the
fences it updates, and presents nothing. The first such frame is logged ("Present: the layer
gave no drawable; frames without one are skipped").

LOCAL TO THIS PORT, NOT FOR DXMT. Applied by macos/build-dxmt.sh to
github.com/athei/dxmt at 01e59e9bde030f105937f249afaac92ada01b4d7, after 0001 to 0005.
Written with an AI assistant (Claude). DXMT does not accept contributions made or
co-authored by AI (its CONTRIBUTING.md), so this patch must not be sent to it as a pull
request. What was found may be reported to its developers, for them to write their own fix;
this patch leaves here when the pinned commit has one.
---
diff --git a/src/dxmt/dxmt_context.cpp b/src/dxmt/dxmt_context.cpp
index f2634d8..79d171e 100644
--- a/src/dxmt/dxmt_context.cpp
+++ b/src/dxmt/dxmt_context.cpp
@@ -1389,10 +1389,20 @@ ArgumentEncodingContext::flushCommands(WMT::CommandBuffer cmdbuf, uint64_t seqId
       );
       auto t1 = clock::now();
       currentFrameStatistics().drawable_blocking_interval += (t1 - t0);
-      if (data->after > 0)
+      if (drawable.handle == NULL_OBJECT_HANDLE) {
+        // no drawable this frame: later encoders still wait for the fences this one updates
+        static bool reported = false;
+        if (!std::exchange(reported, true))
+          WARN("Present: the layer gave no drawable; frames without one are skipped");
+        auto encoder = cmdbuf.blitCommandEncoder();
+        data->fence_wait.forEach([&](auto id) { encoder.waitForFence(fence_pool_[id]); });
+        data->fence_update.forEach([&](auto id) { encoder.updateFence(fence_pool_[id]); });
+        encoder.endEncoding();
+      } else if (data->after > 0) {
         cmdbuf.presentDrawableAfterMinimumDuration(drawable, data->after);
-      else
+      } else {
         cmdbuf.presentDrawable(drawable);
+      }
       data->~PresentData();
       break;
     }
diff --git a/src/dxmt/dxmt_presenter.cpp b/src/dxmt/dxmt_presenter.cpp
index fef1fd4..ba583b9 100644
--- a/src/dxmt/dxmt_presenter.cpp
+++ b/src/dxmt/dxmt_presenter.cpp
@@ -173,6 +173,10 @@ Presenter::encodeCommands(
     std::function<void(WMT::RenderCommandEncoder)> &&update_fences
 ) {
   auto drawable = layer_.nextDrawable();
+  // macOS has no drawable for a layer of no size, or when nextDrawable timed out: encode
+  // nothing, and the caller keeps the frame's fences without presenting
+  if (unlikely(drawable.handle == NULL_OBJECT_HANDLE))
+    return drawable;
 
   WMTRenderPassInfo info;
   WMT::InitializeRenderPassInfo(info);
